HDD vs SSD - side by side 
===========================================================================

                HDD (old school)        |  SSD (the fast one)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SPEED           slow - has a spinning   |  fast - no moving parts, just
                 disk + a little arm    |  memory chips, 
                 that moves to read/    |  almost instantly.
                 write data             |
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DURABILITY       not tough enough       |  way more solid - no moving
                 and the spinning disk  |  parts so it can take bumps,
                 can get damaged, real  |  drops, getting shaken around
                 risk of losing data    |  in a bag etc
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
NOISE           makes noise that        |  silent, no clicking/whirring
                 clicking/whirring      |  at all
                 sound old PCs make     |
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
POWER USE       uses more battery/      |  uses less power, more
                 power                  |  efficient
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRICE           cheaper for lots of     |  pricier per GB, but prices
                 storage (good for      |  have dropped a lot recently
                 2TB+ needs)            |
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
USAGE           best for storing data   |  best for gaming and high performace          
                 servers/data centers   |  faster load times matter
                 for cheap bulk storage |  for gaming), thin/light
                                        |  ultrabooks
===========================================================================


- need speed + something durable for everyday use -> SSD
- need cheap + massive storage,-> HDD

(most new laptops just come with SSD now tbh, HDDs are mostly for
backup/extra storage at this point)
